  "description": "YAVYOM crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C79 H139 Eu5 N2 O42 P6,5(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Eu2 (Eu) has 7 O neighbors; Eu3 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu1 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu5 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu4 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 3 pairs, 3 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.905-3.956 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 105.97-109.04°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Eu5(μ3-OH)(NO3)2(dipp)6(CH3OH)7(H2O)4]·5CH3OH. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula). Article name explicitly identifies I(II).",
